Cosmopolitan exposes _POSIX_VDISABLE as a runtime `extern const int` (its
termios layer normalizes it across hosts), not a compile-time constant. tcsh
seeds the file-scope `ttychars[]` array with it, which needs a constant
expression ("unable to substitute constant"). Pin it to cosmo's runtime value
(0, measured with a cosmocc probe) right after ed.init.c's includes, so the
initializer is constant and the runtime remap that compares ttychars against
_POSIX_VDISABLE still matches. Inert outside Cosmopolitan.

--- a/ed.init.c
+++ b/ed.init.c
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@
 #include "ed.h"
 #include "tc.h"
 #include "ed.defns.h"
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+# undef _POSIX_VDISABLE
+# define _POSIX_VDISABLE 0
+#endif
 
 /* ed.init.c -- init routines for the line editor */
 /* #define DEBUG_TTY */
